test: my aussie pen pal says xmas is in summer there?? that's wrong innit | No, it's right, their summer is December to February | Yes, Christmas is always in winter | Yes, she's joking | It's spring there at Christmas, summer comes in March
test: uk friend's party on 3/4, is that march? | No, in the UK 3/4 means 3 April | Yes, it's March 4 everywhere | It means 4 March in the UK | It's the 34th day of the year
explain: A boy in Colorado set off on a hike at three in the afternoon in winter; darkness came at five, he lost the trail and had to be found by a rescue team.
explain: A girl in Australia called Mia forgot to check the time and missed the last bus home from town; she was stuck at the stop after dark until her parents could drive out.
fact: In winter it gets dark early, and walks that start late can end in the dark, cold and lost.
fact: Checking times and planning ahead stops you being stranded alone at night.
fact: If you are ever stuck alone after dark, phone your parent, or the emergency number if you feel unsafe; never walk off alone or take a lift from a stranger.
