exam: Identify which hand of an analogue clock shows the hour. | The short hand | The long hand | The thinnest hand | The red hand
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises daylight saving time? | Clocks go forward one hour in spring and back in autumn | Clocks go back one hour in spring and forward in autumn | Clocks change by one day each season | Clocks change only in the southern hemisphere
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the date written 3/4 in the United Kingdom. | It signifies the third of April | It signifies the fourth of March | It signifies the third quarter of the year | It signifies a fraction of a day
exam: Ascertain the number of days in the month of November. | Thirty | Thirty-one | Twenty-eight | Twenty-nine
